## Summary

Fixes #36220.

The ERPNext node's `document: create` and `document: update` operations both already try to give a friendly error when the user leaves **Properties** empty:

```ts
const properties = this.getNodeParameter('properties', i) as DocumentProperties;

if (!properties.customProperty.length) {
	throw new NodeOperationError(
		this.getNode(),
		'Please enter at least one property for the document to create.',
		{ itemIndex: i },
	);
}
